  "body": "## What changed\n\n- The viewport's nav column gets a **Pick through** button after Axes, off by default and drawn as off. Clicking it flips `State::pick_through`; the status line reads \"Pick through: on\" / \"Pick through: off\".\n- `feature_click::query_at` now sends `through: state.pick_through` (was always `false`). With the toggle off nothing changes.\n- The toggle is view state like Wire/Paths/Axes, not a command (see `docs/decisions/692-pick-through-mode.md`). No MCP tool: it is a viewport display toggle, not model data.\n- `viewcube::pick_through_label` gives the plain-English state text.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`egui_app::tests::pick_through::*` (new file `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/pick_through.rs`):\n- `the_pick_through_button_is_off_by_default_and_labelled_in_plain_english`\n- `the_toggle_flips_twice_back_to_off_and_queues_no_command`\n- `with_the_toggle_off_a_click_over_a_hidden_edge_never_picks_the_edge`\n- `with_the_toggle_on_a_click_over_a_hidden_edge_reaches_the_far_side_edge`\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` green; `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -D warnings` clean. No snapshot PNG changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Nothing was looked at on screen: the button's position, glyph and on/off drawing were not seen in a running app.\n- Pixel snapshot goldens (release lane) were not run.\n- The nav buttons have no hover tooltip on main, so the label reaches the user through the status line only.\n\n## Notes for reviewers\n\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/viewcube.rs` is now about 478 lines (it was 459 on main, already past the 400-line guide). Splitting it is left for a separate change so this PR stays small.\n- The nav column is one button taller; a pane at the minimum height (260 px) may clip the sixth button, which then takes no clicks.\n- PR #1203 moves these buttons into a bottom bar. This PR stays on main's nav column, so the later merge is a `NAVS` move.\n- Circle and arc centre picks wait for #759, and the maintainer's hand check of viewport picks is still owed. Neither is touched here.\n\nChangelog: Viewport \"Pick through\" toggle (off by default) lets clicks reach edges and points behind the near surface (#692, PR #1204).\n\nRefs #692\n",
